From: Camera firmware maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] avutil/encryption_info: tolerate absent key array during cleanup

av_encryption_init_info_alloc records num_key_ids before checking whether the
key_ids allocation succeeded. Its error cleanup must therefore tolerate a
NULL key_ids pointer with a nonzero count. The allocator also intentionally
leaves that pointer NULL when key_id_size is zero.

Only walk individual key allocations when the array exists. All other owned
fields and list nodes are still released. Deterministic allocator failures at
all six allocation sites and zero-key-size/count controls cover this path.
This does not change the serialization contract or claim a complete fix for
the separately tracked MOV CPU-complexity condition.

Upstream-Status: Pending [local allocation-failure cleanup correction]

--- a/libavutil/encryption_info.c
+++ b/libavutil/encryption_info.c
@@ -221,7 +221,7 @@ void av_encryption_init_info_free(AVEncryptionInitInfo *info)
         AVEncryptionInitInfo *next = info->next;
         uint32_t i;
 
-        for (i = 0; i < info->num_key_ids; i++) {
+        for (i = 0; info->key_ids && i < info->num_key_ids; i++) {
             av_free(info->key_ids[i]);
         }
         av_free(info->system_id);
